// Composed counts, for the many passes that walk a function's blocks or a
// block's instructions with `while(i < len(...(x)))`. A call may not sit
// inside a call's argument, so the length needs a name -- but naming it once
// before the loop would freeze it, and a pass that pushes or kills an
// instruction mid-walk needs the count read fresh on every iteration.

blk_count(int f) {
  int[] blks = (import fnblk)[f];
  int n = len(blks);
} return int n;
given ir_rows (0):(1)
given cfg_fixture (0):(2)
given ir_rows (1):(1)

